Subject: [PATCH] mountmgr: report the real removability and bus type in
 StorageDeviceProperty

query_property() answers IOCTL_STORAGE_QUERY_PROPERTY with a comment that says
"Faking StorageDeviceProperty data" and then reports RemovableMedia = FALSE and
BusType = BusTypeScsi for every device on the system -- including CD-ROMs and
USB sticks.

Those two fields are the ones applications actually read, and "a fixed SCSI
disk" is a worse answer than none: an application that lists removable devices
filters them out. mountmgr already knows what kind of device this is -- it is
how GetDriveType() tells a stick from a hard disk -- so it can say so.

Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18, whose EXPORT-mode "Devices" browser stays empty
for a FAT32 USB stick while the "Explorer" browser beside it correctly lists the
fixed drives.

The rest of the descriptor is left alone; this only stops the two fields that are
knowably wrong from being knowably wrong.

---
--- a/dlls/mountmgr.sys/device.c
+++ b/dlls/mountmgr.sys/device.c
@@ -1580,6 +1580,37 @@
             descriptor->ProductRevisionOffset = 0;
             descriptor->BusType = BusTypeScsi;
             descriptor->RawPropertiesLength = 0;
+
+            /* RBW-BUSTYPE: the two fields above are the ones applications
+             * actually read, and answering "a fixed SCSI disk" for every device
+             * is worse than answering nothing. We already know what kind of
+             * device this is -- it is why GetDriveType() can tell a stick from a
+             * hard disk -- so say so.
+             *
+             * Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18: its EXPORT-mode "Devices" browser
+             * stays empty for a removable FAT32 stick that is correctly reported
+             * as DRIVE_REMOVABLE, while the "Explorer" browser beside it lists
+             * the fixed drives. Windows reports BusTypeUsb and RemovableMedia
+             * TRUE for a USB mass-storage stick. */
+            switch (device->type)
+            {
+            case DEVICE_HARDDISK:   /* a removable disk: in practice, a USB stick */
+                descriptor->RemovableMedia = TRUE;
+                descriptor->BusType = BusTypeUsb;
+                break;
+            case DEVICE_FLOPPY:
+                descriptor->RemovableMedia = TRUE;
+                break;
+            case DEVICE_CDROM:
+            case DEVICE_DVD:
+                descriptor->RemovableMedia = TRUE;
+                descriptor->BusType = BusTypeAtapi;
+                break;
+            default:
+                break;
+            }
+            TRACE( "RBW-BUSTYPE device type %u -> removable %u bus %u\n",
+                   device->type, descriptor->RemovableMedia, descriptor->BusType );
             if (!device->serial) descriptor->SerialNumberOffset = 0;
             else
             {
